CORE
main.c
--dump-c
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^  (struct|union) \{.*\$pad
--
This test should be run via chain.sh, which will try to recompile the dumped C
code. dump-c prints the types of members of anonymous struct or union type as
inline definitions, which must not include the padding components, as these
are not part of the source program and the compiler adds the same padding.
